Provide a complete Scaladoc with the method signature, a clear description of its role in implicit resolution, and an `@return` tag. Example: 'implicit def fallbackNotGiven[T]: NotGiven[T] = new NotGiven[T]()

Provides a fallback instance of `NotGiven[T]` for any type `T` when no higher-priority implicit is available. This method enables the emulation of negation in Scala 2 by ensuring a `NotGiven[T]` is always available in implicit scope.

@return A `NotGiven[T]` instance for the type `T`.'
